Initially, group B consists of participants with scores ≥65 who are promoted, with an average score of 71. Group C consists of participants with scores <60 who are not promoted, with an average of 56. Group A initially has scores between 60-64, not meeting the passmark, so they are not promoted. After an increase of 5 points to all scores, all participants in groups A and B are promoted, leaving only group C as non-promoted. The overall average before the increase is 66. Group averaging calculations can define the relationships between these groups.

