\begin{tabular}{c c c} $p=(a+b+c)+\left(\dfrac 1a+\dfrac 1b+\dfrac 1c\right)$  & \text{and} &  $q=\dfrac ab+\dfrac bc+\dfrac ca$ .
\end{tabular}
Given that both  $p$  and  $q$  are real numbers, find all possible values of the ordered pair  $(p,q)$ .

*David Altizio*

**Plan:**
```xml
<think>
**Core Principle Identification**: The core principles involve complex numbers with product 1, and the reality of symmetric expressions. Specifically, given \(a \cdot b \cdot c = 1\), we have \(p = (a + b + c) + \left(\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{1}{c}\right) = a + b + c + ab + bc + ca\) (using \(1/a = bc\), etc.). Also, \(q = \frac{a}{b} + \frac{b}{c} + \frac{c}{a}\). The reality of \(p\) and \(q\) imposes conditions on \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\), leading to algebraic constraints that must be satisfied.

